messages:
elaine: Quick heads-up on PR #5299  function-calling examples in the API ref are inconsistent with runtime.
mike: TL;DR what broke for customers?
elaine: The OpenAPI example shows `result` as a single string in the callback payload, but the runtime emits `results` as an array of objects: [{ name, type, value }]. Clients that copy the example fail when they try to call `JSON.parse(result)`.
hannah: Ah ok. SDKs currently map that array to a single `tool_output` string for backward compatibility, which is why our SDK snippets look different from the raw API examples.
prashant: Action items: 1) update OpenAPI example to show the real array-of-objects payload, 2) add a short migration note on the page explaining SDK mapping vs raw API, 3) add a docs unit to validate example shape against the callback schema.
elaine: I'll paste the bad example from the PR so we can be explicit.

```json
// bad example (from PR)
{
  "callback": {
    "id": "cb_123",
    "result": "{\"label\": \"cat\", \"score\": 0.98}"
  }
}
```

mike: That explains the confusion. Runtime actually returns:

```json
// canonical runtime callback
{
  "callback": {
    "id": "cb_123",
    "results": [
      { "name": "label", "type": "string", "value": "cat" },
      { "name": "score", "type": "float", "value": 0.98 }
    ]
  }
}
```

hannah: For SDK snippets we should keep the existing high-level helper example but add a clear raw-API example showing `results` array and a note like: "SDKs may coerce `results` to a convenience string field; raw HTTP callers should parse `results` array."
prashant: I'll patch /openapi/generated.yml to replace the broken example and add an example-validator test that fails CI if the callback example doesn't conform to the callback schema.
doc-bot: CI: preview build for branch fix-fncall-examples -> https://staging-docs.redwood.ai/preview/5299 (lint OK, example-check pending)
elaine: Thanks — once the preview is up I'll review and add a changelog line about clarifying function-calling callback payloads and SDK mapping. Closing after merge.
